{
	title: 'Lazy provider and synthetic model implementations',
	spec: 'Provider implementation code and synthetic model implementations are absent from the normal host startup import graph. Directory-discovered src/host/providers/<name>.ts entries expose lightweight catalog metadata and lazily delegate request, parse and live model discovery to the relevant adapter. Adding a provider entry needs no central startup import or registration edit; reserve implementation helpers outside that directory. Discover filenames without executing every provider entry at initialization, and cache loaded entries using the module loader. Metadata queries, model validation and listing built-in names do not load request/stream implementations. Fetch live catalogs only for configured providers or local endpoints, retaining offline fallbacks and credential-scoped catalog invalidation. A chosen provider alone loads its implementation and transport dependencies; implementations remain loaded for reuse. Keep programmatic provider.register and mutable plugin hooks. Existing Anthropic, OpenAI, OpenRouter, OpenCode Go and Ollama mappings, credentials, effort capabilities and errors stay intact. Synthetic registry callbacks lazily load only the invoked internal model; normal greetings and slash command enumeration must not import intro.ts or other scripted models. Post-intro games remain lazy too. Shared HTTP/SSE validation and cancellation stay unchanged. Retain process-isolated import-boundary coverage proving cold startup/catalog access does not import adapters or intro, selecting one does not import others, and unknown names cannot resolve arbitrary paths. Do not add new providers or an installer: support for broader provider catalogs is future work. This restores the startup invariant that unused model implementations cost no module execution on restart, as requested by Antti.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Entries are lightweight Provider objects with deferred adapter methods. providers.init scans filenames, installs cached property getters, preserves explicit registrations, and includes custom compatible endpoints. Compatible endpoint and capability metadata lives in compat-catalog.ts; existing adapter metadata hooks forward to catalog fields. Model discovery skips unconfigured remote providers; local discovery remains available. Indirect eager imports also existed in greetings, model/intro/plugin-sync commands and plugin-sync handling, not just lifecycle and synthetic. Unknown model names cannot select inherited object properties. Cold-process tests initialize the host, enumerate commands, inspect catalogs, then load individual adapters or a synthetic model without the others.'
	],
